#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate the $4 \\times 4$ lattice {#simulate-the-4-times-4-lattice}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the $4 \\times 4$ lattice, you can do both: compute the exact state at "
"every coupling, and sample every circuit with 10,000 shots, as an experiment"
" would. The shots are stored with shape (batches, shots, qubits), the same "
"layout as the randomizations in the hardware data. Here all 10,000 shots "
"form a single batch, so the bootstrap over batches adds no shot noise, and "
"the error bars in the next plot show only the spread between marginal "
"positions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2. What to measure and how to estimate it {#2-what-to-measure-and-how-to-"
"estimate-it}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The IPR and the collision entropy {#the-ipr-and-the-collision-entropy}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a marginal $A$ of $n_A$ qubits with bitstring distribution $p_A(a)$, the"
" quantity to estimate is the inverse participation ratio (IPR) of the "
"marginal distribution, and from it the collision entropy:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = \\sum_a p_A(a)^2, \\qquad S_2[A] = -\\log_2 \\mathrm{IPR}_A\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is also the probability that two shots agree on the "
"marginal. A product state has $\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 1$, and a random state has "
"$\\mathrm{IPR}_A \\approx 2^{-n_A}$, so $S_2$ climbs from 0 to about $n_A$ "
"bits as the marginal becomes random.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 1: count pairs of shots {#estimator-1-count-pairs-of-shots}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** How do you estimate this quantity from your shots?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The naive estimator computes each $p(a)$ from the shots as $\\hat p(a) = n_a / N$, then sums $\\sum_a \\hat p(a)^2$.\n"
"This estimator is biased.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\sum_a n_a^2 / N^2$ counts every shot as agreeing with itself, which "
"pushes the estimate up: on average it gives $\\mathrm{IPR}_A + (1 - "
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A)/N$ instead of $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$. Since $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is"
" the probability that two shots agree, count only pairs of *different* "
"shots:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{IPR}}_A = \\frac{\\sum_a n_a (n_a - 1)}{N (N - 1)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is unbiased, and it is what `ipr_from_shots` below computes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 2: Parseval expansion {#estimator-2-parseval-expansion}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The IPR can also be written through the parities $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ of "
"all nonempty subsets $S$ of the marginal:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{\\emptyset \\neq S \\subseteq A} \\langle Z_S \\rangle^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This form matters because error mitigation methods such as PEA work on expectation values, not on probabilities.\n"
"**One qubit:** The outcome probabilities are $p(0) = (1 + \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$ and $p(1) = (1 - \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$, so\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = p(0)^2 + p(1)^2 = \\frac{1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"**A $2 \\times 2$ marginal:** With its qubits labeled $a, b, c, d$, the marginal has $2^4 - 1 = 15$ parities: 4 single qubits, 6 pairs, 4 triples, and the whole marginal, so\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = \\frac{1}{16} \\Bigl(1\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\Bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""

